 &lt;BR&gt; 
3. The Group has organised the businesses into two categories viz., Air Compressors and Automotive Equipment. This reporting complies with the Ind AS segment reporting principles. Refer Annexure I attached herewith. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
4. Other Income for the quarter ended September 30, 2025 and nine months ended December 31, 2025 includes sale of properties amounting to Rs. 313 million and Rs. 376 million, respectively. &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
5. On November 21, 2025, the Government of India notified four Labour Codes, effective immediately, replacing the existing 29 labour laws. Implementation of these Codes resulted in a past service liability of Rs. 128 million, and the same has been presented as an Exceptional Item in the Standalone Financial Results for the quarter and nine months ended December 31, 2025. The Company continues to monitor the finalisation of Central and State Rules, as well as Government clarifications on other aspects of the Labour Codes, and will incorporate appropriate accounting treatment based on these developments as required. &lt;BR&gt; 
